<!--
  Status-bar notification icon.

  Android draws notification icons as a MASK: every non-transparent pixel is
  painted in the system tint, colour and detail are discarded. The launcher
  icon is therefore the wrong asset for this — it would render as a solid white
  blob. This is the Chattr speech bubble from assets/icon/foreground.svg as a
  flat silhouette, centred in the 1024 viewport (the mark's own bounds are
  751x629, which leaves the padding a status-bar icon needs).

  It also has to live in `drawable/`, not `mipmap/`: flutter_local_notifications
  resolves the name with getIdentifier(name, "drawable", package) — one lookup,
  drawable only, and the string is taken verbatim. That is why the previous
  value '@mipmap/ic_launcher' failed twice over and left Android with no local
  notifications at all.
-->
